WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.930 --> 00:00:05.770
Inside your skull is about one and a half
kilos of meat that somehow manages to keep

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:09.690
you breathing, help you remember where your
wallet is and remind you which is the best

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:13.110
hole to put your lunch in…err… not that
one.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:17.269
And you know what, maths tests aside, it normally
does a pretty decent job of stuff.

00:00:17.269 --> 00:00:21.190
But when you are dealing with something so
unbelievably complicated, among the billions

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:27.600
of humans all over the planet, you’re occasionally
going to have some pretty unusual brain anomalies.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:32.710
There’s the obvious ones like amnesia and
dyslexia but today we’re looking at naughty

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:43.890
neurons, peculiar pathways and confusing consciousness;
we’re looking at 6 bizarre brain disorders.

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:49.670
Riley Day sounds like an awful 90s pop star
but it’s actually a genetic condition, officially

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:55.410
named Familial dysautonomia, which has the
notable effect of making people unable to

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:56.910
feel pain.

00:00:56.910 --> 00:01:00.610
But if you’re wondering “okay, so where
is this race of super people?”

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:05.540
Well it also causes poor growth, unstable
blood pressure, violent vomiting, pneumonia

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:07.220
and problems with speech and movement.

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:11.830
So, whilst I’m sure they’d love to help
save you from a burning building, they kind

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:13.690
of have their own issues to deal with.

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:17.050
It’s also very unique to one group of people.

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:22.640
The only ever cases of Riley-Day syndrome
have been found in Ashkenazi Jews.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:29.010
Jewish people are, for the most part, split
into 3 ethnic groups; Ashkenazi, Sephardic

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:30.280
and Mizrahi.

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:35.440
Ashkenazi is the biggest group, originally
from Eastern Europe, containing about 11 million

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:38.170
people, half of which live in the US.

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:41.479
To really rub it in, sufferers also don’t
produce tears.

00:01:41.479 --> 00:01:48.130
There’s also an opposite condition; Hyperalgesia,
which is a hyper-sensitivity to pain.

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:52.170
This one’s not genetic though, it can be
caused by long-term opioid use, like with

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:54.650
heroin addiction.

00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:58.010
Next we have Alice in Wonderland Syndrome.

00:01:58.010 --> 00:01:59.010
What do you think this is?

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:00.010
Do you go chasing rabbits?

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:02.490
Do you see smiling cats wherever you go?

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:08.019
No, in this wonderland, you lose control of
your perception of size and things seem all

00:02:08.019 --> 00:02:12.719
out of proportion like you’re Alice, eating
the cake and drinking from the bottle, growing

00:02:12.719 --> 00:02:14.139
and shrinking.

00:02:14.139 --> 00:02:19.529
The medical terms are micropsia and macropsia;
that’s seeing things as small and seeing

00:02:19.529 --> 00:02:21.139
them as big.

00:02:21.139 --> 00:02:26.569
Or you can get pelopsia and teleopsia, where
objects seem nearer or further away.

00:02:26.569 --> 00:02:31.420
Unsurprisingly, this can happen through taking
hallucinogenic drugs but it also affects those

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:34.090
with severe migraines and brain tumors.

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:38.780
Many children experience a form of it at some
point but it disappears in teenage years.

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:44.419
It’s also one of the symptoms of the Epstein–Barr
virus, which is a type of herpes.

00:02:44.419 --> 00:02:49.530
Interestingly, Lewis Carrol was known to suffer
from migraines so perhaps this was his inspiration

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:52.360
for the distorted world down the rabbit hole.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:56.840
I don’t want to know how he got the idea
of an extremely high caterpillar though.

00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:01.659
The Cheshire Cat once said “If you do not
know where you want to go, it doesn’t matter

00:03:01.659 --> 00:03:06.930
which path you take” and this leads us to
our next condition; aboulomania.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:09.049
This is what we call pathological indecisiveness.

00:03:09.049 --> 00:03:14.949
A lot of people say they’re bad at making
decisions and might spend ten minutes gnawing

00:03:14.949 --> 00:03:19.150
at their finger nails as their eyes jump from
chocolate cake to cheesecake… obviously

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:22.949
chocolate cake, you idiot … but this is
much worse than that.

00:03:22.949 --> 00:03:25.989
Decision making involves various parts of
the brain and varies depending on the type

00:03:25.989 --> 00:03:30.309
of choice, for example it’s a different
process for a free choice such as “what’s

00:03:30.309 --> 00:03:31.719
your favourite sandwich?”

00:03:31.719 --> 00:03:35.709
compared to a closed choice such as “beer
or cider”.

00:03:35.709 --> 00:03:40.079
With Aboulomania, the sufferers massively
over-analyze the options, always thinking

00:03:40.079 --> 00:03:46.500
of the worst outcomes and so manage to talk
themselves out of ever doing anything, effectively

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:48.499
becoming socially paralyzed.

00:03:48.499 --> 00:03:50.900
Now let’s talk some sense.

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:55.191
There’s a lot of misunderstanding about
the senses, for example the idea that there

00:03:55.191 --> 00:03:57.279
are only 5 of them.

00:03:57.279 --> 00:04:01.709
What about the sense of balance? of pain?
and proprioception?

00:04:01.709 --> 00:04:05.869
which is an understanding of the relative
positions of your body parts.

00:04:05.869 --> 00:04:11.260
Synesthesia is a condition where perceptions
that are normally separate become mixed, such

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:14.669
as seeing numbers as colours or tasting words.

00:04:14.669 --> 00:04:19.449
There are many different forms but the number-colour
thing is the most common, affecting yellow

00:04:19.449 --> 00:04:22.120
out of purple people with the condition.

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:28.069
Some of the rarer forms of the condition include
seeing time as shapes and feeling other people’s

00:04:28.069 --> 00:04:32.130
sensations, like if you saw someone scratching
their leg, you would immediately feel that

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:36.730
same scratching on your own thigh, it’s
like a hyper form of empathy.

00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:41.639
The list of famous synesthetes, as they’re
called, includes Pharrell Williams, Tesla

00:04:41.639 --> 00:04:47.060
and Kandinsky
Prosopagnosia is an impairment of your facial-recognition

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:50.919
ability, controlled by the fusiform gyrus
in your frontal lobe.

00:04:50.919 --> 00:04:57.169
It can even result in not being able to recognize
your own face, which means you can play Where’s

00:04:57.169 --> 00:04:59.050
Wally with your own family album.

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:04.220
A common issue that most of us have is a difficulty
telling apart people of different races.

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:09.310
And it seems that it’s not that we can’t
tell the difference, it’s just that we don’t.

00:05:09.310 --> 00:05:15.020
Psychologist Daniel Levin puts it like this;
“When a white person looks at another white

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:18.870
person's nose, they're likely to think to
themselves, 'That's John's nose.'

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:24.360
When they look at a black person's nose, they're
likely to think, 'That's a black nose.'"

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:29.550
For your own race you look in a holistic way,
getting an overall impression of it, whereas

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:33.840
with other races you just bounce around the
features, like you’ve not seen a face before

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:36.599
and are trying to understand it.

00:05:36.599 --> 00:05:41.650
Simply because your brain is less use to seeing
faces of other races than of your own.

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:44.710
Obviously this improves dramatically if you
live in a multi-cultural area.

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:50.610
But for those with prosopagnosia, there’s
no real way to improve they’re facial recognitions

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:55.090
abilities, so they have to rely on remembering
people’s dress sense or body language in

00:05:55.090 --> 00:05:58.249
order to distinguish them.

00:05:58.249 --> 00:06:03.090
Not recognizing your own face is one thing
but what about not knowing who is in charge

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:04.780
of your hand?

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:10.909
Alien Hand Syndrome was first documented in
Germany in 1908 and has since been most commonly

00:06:10.909 --> 00:06:17.020
associated with people who’ve had the two
hemispheres of their brain surgically separated,

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:18.370
often as a cure for epilepsy.

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:23.000
But it can also occur after various brain
conditions like Alzheimer’s, tumors and

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:24.139
so on.

00:06:24.139 --> 00:06:30.319
With Alien Hand Syndrome, one hand moves purposefully,
seemingly of its own will and the owner of

00:06:30.319 --> 00:06:33.490
the hand can do nothing to stop it no matter
how hard they try.

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:37.999
If there are any bosses watching who have
had a sexual harassment allegation made against

00:06:37.999 --> 00:06:42.560
them, don’t try to use Alien Hand Syndrome
as an excuse, you are just a creep and you

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:44.449
deserve to be fired.

00:06:44.449 --> 00:06:49.270
The brain is unbelievably complicated and
we never know what unusual brain syndrome

00:06:49.270 --> 00:06:51.580
will manifest itself, out of the blue.

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:55.860
So, if you’re worried that you’ll never
stop smoking weed in your bedroom, playing

00:06:55.860 --> 00:07:00.319
Call of Duty and skipping on the housework,
maybe just keep sticking it out until the

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:06.600
world finally recognizes your “Faulty-Motivational-Syndrome”
and you might get the sympathy you richly

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:33.770
deserve.

